{:id "0029-lab-renderer"
 :title "Lab page: type into letters in 3D space (three.js, WebGPU with WebGL2 fallback)"
 :lupa/deps #{"0026-lab-draft" "0027-lab-cues" "0028-lab-poses"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "public/lab/index.html is a playable prototype: you type into what
        looks like a dark stage and your letters spring into 3D space,
        finished words play their cues (lightning for 'crash', a launch for
        'ship', a shimmer for 'hallucination'), and backspaced letters drift
        off as embers. It renders with WebGPU where the browser has it and
        WebGL2 otherwise, and it says which. The pure core (draft, cues,
        poses) does all the deciding; this order only wires input and draws
        frames."
 :scope ["public/lab/index.html" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
         "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "shadow-cljs.edn" "package.json"
         "package-lock.json" "bb.edn" "src/halfahead/dev/lab.clj"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Read docs/LAB.md first (the seam), then the three pure namespaces.

          Dependencies (package.json, exact versions, lock regenerated with
          npm install against the committed lock): three 0.187.0 and
          @mapbox/tiny-sdf 2.3.0. Nothing else.

          shadow-cljs.edn: a new :lab build (:target :browser, output
          public/lab/js, asset-path \"js\", init halfahead.lab.main/init!).
          Do not change the :app or :test builds.

          public/lab/index.html: a full-viewport <canvas> (aria-hidden) on a
          dark background, a real <textarea> labelled 'Type here' laid over
          it, focused on load, with transparent text and caret (it is the
          input: IME, paste, undo and screen readers keep working), a small
          status line naming the backend, and a link back to the app.

          halfahead.lab.main (cljs shell): one atom {:draft ..}. On every
          input event: (lab.draft/edit draft value (js/performance.now)
          lab.cues/word-cue). A requestAnimationFrame loop computes
          (lab.pose/frame (lab.draft/prune draft now) now opts) and hands it
          to the renderer; opts carry the renderer's advance function, a
          width that fits the viewport, and :reduced-motion? from
          matchMedia (re-read on change). Expose window.__lab with: backend
          (\"WebGPU\" or \"WebGL2\"), liveText() (the live poses' chars
          joined), lastFrame() (the last frame as JS), and drawn() (glyph
          instances drawn in the last frame).

          halfahead.lab.render (cljs; the only namespace that touches
          three.js or the GPU):
          - A WebGPURenderer from \"three/webgpu\"; it falls back to WebGL2
            when WebGPU is unavailable; report which backend is active.
          - A perspective camera looking at the text plane from slightly
            below and in front, so z motion reads as depth.
          - A glyph atlas built at start with @mapbox/tiny-sdf from a CSS
            font stack (a sans in the label style; no font files), growing
            lazily for characters not yet in it; expose (advance char) from
            the glyph metrics, in em.
          - One InstancedMesh of quads, one instance per pose; per-instance
            attributes for the atlas rectangle, opacity, glow and wobble;
            instance matrices from x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, scale.
          - Material: alpha from the signed distance field with a smooth
            edge; glow as a soft halo from the same field, tinted warm (the
            vermilion of the app's palette); wobble as a jelly deformation
            of the quad's vertices, sin of time and vertex position times
            the wobble amplitude. Ghosts tinted ember orange.
          - The caret as a thin bar at the frame's caret position.
          If TSL node materials prove unworkable in this three.js version,
          use WebGLRenderer with a GLSL ShaderMaterial instead and say so in
          the final message; the frame contract does not change.
          Only draw frames; decide nothing.

          src/halfahead/dev/lab.clj and bb.edn: `bb lab` compiles :lab,
          serves public/ with halfahead.dev.serve on a free port and prints
          the URL of /lab/; `bb lab:e2e` runs e2e/lab.mjs against it and
          stops the server by its handle.

          e2e/lab.mjs (Playwright): open /lab/; wait for window.__lab;
          assert backend is WebGPU or WebGL2; type \"we finally shipped it!
          then a crash \" with 70 ms between keys; 300 ms later screenshot
          out/lab/typing-mid.png; assert __lab.liveText() equals the
          textarea's value and __lab.drawn() >= its length; press Backspace
          three times, 100 ms later screenshot out/lab/embers.png and
          assert lastFrame() has ghost poses; wait 2 s, screenshot
          out/lab/settled.png and assert no ghosts and every live pose has
          scale 1; repeat the typing in a context with reducedMotion
          'reduce' and assert every live pose is at scale 1 immediately.

          docs/LAB.md: keep the foreman's text; add a 'Running it' section."
 :acceptance
 ["`bb lab:e2e` passes in this container and the final message lists the
   three screenshots (the foreman will look at them) and the backend the
   headless browser used"
  "`bb test` stays green; the :app build and the main page are unchanged"
  "The canvas is aria-hidden and the textarea is a real, labelled, focused
   input (assert in e2e: the focused element is the textarea)"]
 :non-goals
 ["No changes to lab.draft, lab.cues, lab.pose, the glossary, the schema,
   or the app"
  "No models, sound, or network; no fonts downloaded"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play` (fixed emulator ports)"]
 :context ["docs/LAB.md" "src/halfahead/lab/draft.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/cues.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "src/halfahead/dev/serve.clj"
           "e2e/smoke.mjs" "shadow-cljs.edn" "bb.edn" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
